ui.helpTitle=Radeoner — help
ui.helpText=Radeoner {0} — lightweight AMD GPU panel.\n\nTab / Shift+Tab: fields and buttons.\nCtrl+Tab: tabs.\nF5: refresh. F6: last message.\nCtrl+Enter: apply changes.\nCtrl+E: export JSON. Ctrl+I: import JSON.\nCtrl+Shift+S: save report. F1: help.\n\nAlt+F4 and the close button hide to the tray. Exit in the window or tray menu closes the program completely. Launching the EXE again shows the existing window.\n\nProfiles save editor values. Import checks the GPU model, ranges and units and fills the fields. Only Apply sends changes to the driver.\n\nPersonalization: language from lang/*.lng, theme, text size and optional startup to the tray. Preferences are saved next to the EXE. Startup does not apply a GPU profile.\n\nSensors and tray readings update in the background when updates are enabled. You can disable this to reduce waking the GPU. Missing readings are marked.\n\nFields have names and units for NVDA. Copy readings and reports using Ctrl+A, Ctrl+C. Features depend on the GPU and driver. Exiting does not undo values already written to the driver. Updates tab: check at startup and at a chosen interval; Download and install updates the application. See Readme.en.txt for details.
